The page map covers the arenas where address space is kept aside.

The page map has a part of 64 KiB for every 512 MiB of addresses, taken from
the system when a page in that range is first registered. An arena is reserved
wherever the system puts it, so it can lie across the end of such a range.
When the address space has run out by then, no page beyond that end can be
registered, and what the arena holds there cannot be handed out. It all becomes
available the moment one request gets the 64 KiB.

Where an embedder keeps address space aside
(ask-who-may-take-address-space.patch), the parts of the page map for the
arenas are made ahead: for the arenas that are there when the keeper is
registered, and for each later one when it is reserved. Not for exclusive
arenas, which can be far larger than what is ever used of them.

